cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "benchLANG: Reproducible Programming Language Performance Benchmark"
message: "If you use these results, please cite this repository."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Gleb
    family-names: Olsen
repository-code: "https://github.com/glebolsen/benchLANG"
abstract: >-
  Cross-language runtime benchmark covering 20 programming languages
  (C, C++, Rust, Zig, Go, Nim, Fortran, Ada, D, Swift, Haskell, Java, C#,
  OCaml, Dart, Pascal, JS Bun/Node, PHP, Python CPython/PyPy3, Ruby) on six
  workloads: trial division primes, recursive Fibonacci, string equality,
  Mandelbrot, binary trees and k-nucleotide. Records per-workload wall time,
  process CPU time, peak memory usage, native binary size and compile time,
  and verifies identical checksums across languages.
  Toolchains pinned via Nix flake for reproducibility.
keywords:
  - benchmark
  - programming-languages
  - performance
  - language-comparison
  - reproducible-benchmarks
license: MIT
version: "2026.10"
date-released: "2026-10-20"
